The CODE in this repository is MIT, as above.

The CORPUS is not. Everything under src/content/ and corpus/ — the chains, the
arbitrations, and the reasoning in them — is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

That split is deliberate. The arbitration is the only part of this project a
fork does not get for free, and share-alike is what stops it being absorbed
into a closed catalogue. See DESIGN.md, Decisions Log.
